<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharafnama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1597</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sharafnama is a history of the Kurdish dynasties and principalities written in Persian by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharaf-khan-bidlisi">Sharaf Khan Bidlisi</a>, emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bitlis">Bitlis</a>, and completed in 1597. It surveys the ruling families of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurdistan">Kurdistan</a>, their genealogies and their relations with the Ottoman and Safavid empires, and adds a chronicle of Ottoman and Persian rulers. It is the principal source for the history of the Kurdish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a>.</p></div>
<section><h2 class="enc-section-title">Mentioned in 2 state histories</h2><div class="enc-mentions"><a href="/state/emirate-of-bitlis">Emirate of Bitlis</a><a href="/state/soran-emirate">Soran emirate</a></div></section>
